From: Yu Zhao <yuzhao@google.com>
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] mm: mglru: avoid scan counter underflow on retry

Adapted from upstream commit
8b671fe1a879923ecfb72dda6caf01460dd885ef.

A page rejected by trylock_page() was not counted by shrink_page_list().
Subtracting it before a clean-page retry can underflow nr_scanned and
subsequently cause division by zero in vmpressure_calc_level(). Keep the
scan counter monotonic, as upstream does for folio-based reclaim.

Adaptation: remove the equivalent thp_nr_pages() subtraction from the
page-based Android 5.15 evict_pages(). No vendor hook, ABI or policy
change is introduced.
The original upstream authorship trailers are retained below; they are
not new sign-offs made on behalf of these contributors.

Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/8b671fe1a879923ecfb72dda6caf01460dd885ef
Signed-off-by: Yu Zhao <yuzhao@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -4914,9 +4914,8 @@
 		}
 
 		/* retry pages that may have missed rotate_reclaimable_page() */
 		list_move(&page->lru, &clean);
-		sc->nr_scanned -= thp_nr_pages(page);
 	}
 
 	spin_lock_irq(&lruvec->lru_lock);
 
